   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On Fri, 2015-08-28 at 08:38 -0700, Marco Helbich wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hello, \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I am running a spatial varying coefficients model in R-INLA. I am\r<br>&gt; wondering how to plot the varying parameters across space. The paper\r<br>&gt; by Martino and Rue (2010)‎ only shows the final map but unfortunately\r<br>&gt; not how to get there. \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Any answer is highly appreciated.\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "run \r<br>\r<br>\tdemo(Bym)\r<br>\r<br>this contain the code for the function\r<br>\r<br>\tBym.map(...)\r<br>\r<br>which you run with result$summary.random$region.x$mean\r<br>\r<br>for example\r<br>\r<br>H\r<br>\r<br>-- \r<br>Håvard Rue\r<br><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">he...@r-inla.org</a>\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
