   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Many thanks Håvard! It works perfectly. I was not aware of this function... <br><br>Btw, ?Bym.map gives the following: <br><br><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"color:blue\">?Bym.map\r\n</span>No documentation for ‘Bym.map’ in specified packages and libraries:\r\nyou could try ‘??Bym.map’</pre></span><br>Marco</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>Am Freitag, 28. August 2015 17:54:40 UTC+2 schrieb help help:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">On Fri, 2015-08-28 at 08:38 -0700, Marco Helbich wrote:\r\n<br>&gt; Hello, \r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; I am running a spatial varying coefficients model in R-INLA. I am\r\n<br>&gt; wondering how to plot the varying parameters across space. The paper\r\n<br>&gt; by Martino and Rue (2010)‎ only shows the final map but unfortunately\r\n<br>&gt; not how to get there. \r\n<br>&gt; \r\n<br>&gt; Any answer is highly appreciated.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>run \r\n<br>\r\n<br>        demo(Bym)\r\n<br>\r\n<br>this contain the code for the function\r\n<br>\r\n<br>        Bym.map(...)\r\n<br>\r\n<br>which you run with result$summary.random$region.x$mean\r\n<br>\r\n<br>for example\r\n<br>\r\n<br>H\r\n<br>\r\n<br>-- \r\n<br>Håvard Rue\r\n<br><a rel=\"nofollow\">he...@r-inla.org</a>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br></blockquote></div>"
